;; Versioned migration.
;; There is no photo library: a picture (:photo/*) always belongs to exactly one product through its
;; :product-image/ entry. Making the :product-image/photo reference a component means that removing a
;; picture from its product (or retracting the product-image entity) retracts the photo record with it, so
;; no unassigned photo record can exist. The library endpoints and their code are removed in the same release.
{:id :0010-pictures-belong-to-products,
 :description "Product pictures own their photo record (no photo library)",
 :tx-data
 [{:db/ident :product-image/photo,
   :db/isComponent true}]}
